Rule 1 (tensor shape matches given tuple shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= ndim(v_1) = v_2.len ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = v_2[i]
>>
Rule 2 (tensor has at least one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 6 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) - 1
